+/*
+ * xemu-ps4: the ahead-of-time translator's runtime (see include/exec/aot.h).
+ *
+ * Recording: tcg_gen_code hands every translated block to aot_record_tb, which writes
+ * it as C (tcg/tcg-aot.c.inc) into /data/xemu/aot/<title ID>/blocks-<n>.c through a
+ * writer thread, with the ABI header (aot_abi.h) the PC's build includes.
+ *
+ * Running: /data/xemu/aot/<title ID>.aot is an x86-64 ELF shared object made by
+ * scripts/aot-build.py (clang, position-independent, no imports). It is mapped into
+ * executable memory here, its relative relocations applied and its helper imports
+ * resolved by name. Its header lists the blocks (pc, flags, cflags, size, code hash);
+ * when the JIT is about to translate one of them and the guest's code bytes still
+ * hash the same, x86_translate_code makes a one-instruction "trampoline" TB that
+ * calls helper_aot_run, which runs the compiled block. Compiled blocks jump to each
+ * other directly (tail calls) while they stay valid: a block is valid once its
+ * trampoline ran in the current generation; the generation moves on whenever a TLB
+ * flush touches a page holding valid blocks or the TB cache is flushed, and a block
+ * whose trampoline TB is invalidated (its code bytes written) is invalid at once.
+ *
+ * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under
+ * the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by the Free Software
+ * Foundation; either version 2 of the License, or (at your option) any later
+ * version.
+ */
+
