+/*
+ * xemu-ps4: the TLB dirty index. NV2A clears guest RAM's dirty bits for every vertex buffer and
+ * texture the emulated CPU rewrote - several times a draw - and each clear made tlb_reset_dirty
+ * walk every entry of every TLB (up to 2^20 each) under the TLB lock, which the emulated CPU needs
+ * for every TLB fill: v00.15's busiest QEMU function after the JIT. The walk only has to find the
+ * entries that let writes to the pages through without the dirty trap ("writable-clean"). Those
+ * are noted here, per guest RAM page, at the three places an entry becomes so (tlb_set_page_full,
+ * tlb_set_dirty, victim_tlb_hit's swap - all under the TLB lock, as tlb_reset_dirty is), and a
+ * reset visits just those plus the 8-entry victim TLBs. A page with more entries than fit falls
+ * back to the full walk. Stale notes are harmless: each entry is checked before it is changed.
+ */
+#define TDI_SLOTS 4
+#define TDI_OVERFLOW 0xff
